{"book":10,"chapter":29,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE STANDARD LIBRARY / CHAPTER 29","slides":[{"title":"The language's vocabulary","sub":"Chapter 29 · Trait catalog","short":"Intro","main":"Trait groups, and when to derive or impl.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Vocabulary","Groups","derive or by hand"],"captions":["Parameter bounds describe what a function needs from a type","Copying, comparison, conversions, deref, iteration, closures, errors, markers","What a trait promises, when it is derived, and when written by hand"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn f<T: Clone + Debug + Ord>(x: T)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Clone","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Eq / Ord","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"From","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Iterator","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"#[derive(…)]","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"impl … for …","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[19.0,32.4]}]},{"title":"Copying","sub":"Clone, Copy, Drop","short":"Copying","main":"Explicit copy, bitwise copy, release.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Clone","Copy","Drop"],"captions":["Clone is an explicit copy: the call is visible and may be costly","Copy: trivial copying; assignment does not move; all fields Copy and no Drop","Drop frees on destruction: automatic, never called by hand (only drop(x))"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let b = a.clone();"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"i32, char, bool\nCopy","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"String, Vec\nnot Copy","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["impl Drop for File {","    fn drop(&mut self) { /* close */ }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[16.6,31.8]}]},{"title":"Comparison","sub":"Eq, Ord, Hash","short":"Comparison","main":"Partial and total; Hash agrees with Eq.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["PartialEq and Eq","PartialOrd and Ord","Hash"],"captions":["PartialEq: == and !=; Eq is total (x == x): f64 lacks it because of NaN","PartialOrd: order may be undefined; Ord is total: needed for sort, BTreeMap, BinaryHeap","Hash agrees with Eq: equal values, equal hash, or HashMap loses keys"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"f64\nPartialEq","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"i32\nEq","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"f64\nPartialOrd","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"i32, String\nOrd","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[derive(PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash)]","struct Key(u32, String);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.0,28.2]}]},{"title":"Default","sub":"Default values","short":"Default","main":"derive, manual impl, ..Default::default().","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Default","derive","..Default::default()"],"captions":["Default::default(): 0, empty string, empty vector, false: a sensible value","#[derive(Default)] if all fields are Default; by hand for special settings","Config { port: 80, ..Default::default() } fills the rest; unwrap_or_default, or_default"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"0","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"\"\"","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"vec![]","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"false","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[derive(Default)]","struct Config { port: u16, name: String }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["Config { port: 80, ..Default::default() }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[9.6,30.5]}]},{"title":"Conversions","sub":"From, TryFrom, AsRef","short":"Conversions","main":"From and Into, TryFrom, AsRef, Borrow, ToOwned, Cow.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["From and Into","TryFrom, AsRef, Borrow","ToOwned and Cow"],"captions":["From<A> for B is infallible conversion; Into comes for free","TryFrom can fail; AsRef and AsMut: \"as a reference to another type\"; Borrow agrees with Hash and Eq","ToOwned makes an owning version; Cow postpones copying until needed"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["impl From<u8> for Level { … }","let l: Level = 3u8.into();"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"TryFrom","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"AsRef","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Borrow","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn f(s: &str) -> Cow<str> {","    if ok { Cow::Borrowed(s) } else { Cow::Owned(fix(s)) }","}"],"lang":"rust","size":8.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[16.0,25.1]}]},{"title":"Strings","sub":"FromStr and ToString","short":"Strings","main":"parse, to_string, formatting traits.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["FromStr","ToString","Other formats"],"captions":["FromStr gives s.parse::<T>(); the error is the associated type Err","ToString is automatic for any type with Display","LowerHex, UpperHex, Binary, Octal, LowerExp, Pointer: for {:x}, {:X}, {:b}, {:o}, {:e}, {:p}"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["impl FromStr for Point { … }","let p: Point = \"1,2\".parse()?;"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Display","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"to_string()","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"{:x}","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"{:b}","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"{:o}","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"{:e}","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.9,28.4]}]},{"title":"Deref and Index","sub":"Smart references","short":"Deref","main":"Deref coercion; Index.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Deref","Coercion","Index"],"captions":["Deref makes a type a smart reference: Box<T>, Rc<T>, String → str, Vec<T> → [T]","The compiler applies Deref itself where another reference is needed: &String → &str, &Vec<T> → &[T]","Index and IndexMut: square brackets; don't use Deref to fake inheritance"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"String","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"str","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn f(s: &str) { }","f(&String::from(\"a\"));   // &String → &str"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["impl Index<usize> for Row { … }","let x = row[2];"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[16.0,27.1]}]},{"title":"Iteration","sub":"Iterator and relatives","short":"Iteration","main":"IntoIterator, FromIterator, Extend, DoubleEnded.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Iterator","IntoIterator, FromIterator","Relatives"],"captions":["Iterator: one method next() gives dozens of ready ones","IntoIterator: for loops; FromIterator: collect; Extend: add to an existing collection","DoubleEndedIterator (rev), ExactSizeIterator (len), Sum and Product for your types"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["impl Iterator for Count {","    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<…> { … }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"for x in c","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"collect()","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"extend()","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"rev","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"len","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"sum","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"product","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.9,31.6]}]},{"title":"Closures","sub":"Fn, FnMut, FnOnce","short":"Closures","main":"Three traits and their strictness order.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["FnOnce","FnMut","Fn"],"captions":["FnOnce: callable once, takes the captured values","FnMut: callable many times, changes state","Fn: many times, changes nothing; take the loosest fit in a parameter; Box<dyn Fn> to store"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":200.0,"h":40.0,"text":"FnOnce\ntakes","tone":"red","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":200.0,"h":40.0,"text":"FnMut\nchanges state","tone":"yellow","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":200.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Fn\nonly reads","tone":"green","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.3,26.3]}]},{"title":"Errors","sub":"Error","short":"Errors","main":"source, Box<dyn Error>, thiserror, anyhow.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Error","Box<dyn Error>","thiserror, anyhow"],"captions":["Error needs Display and Debug; source() is the cause, so errors form a chain","Box<dyn Error + Send + Sync> takes any; ? converts errors through From","thiserror for libraries; anyhow for applications: a universal error with context"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["impl std::error::Error for MyError {","    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn Error + 'static)> { … }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":8.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn run() -> Result<(), Box<dyn Error>> { … }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"thiserror\nlibraries","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"anyhow\napplications","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.1,23.7]}]},{"title":"Markers","sub":"Send, Sync, Sized","short":"Markers","main":"Send, Sync, Sized, PhantomData.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Send and Sync","Sized","PhantomData"],"captions":["Send: can move to another thread; Sync: can be shared between threads; both automatic","Rc is not Send (non-atomic counter); Arc and Mutex are Send + Sync; Sized: size known, ?Sized: slices","PhantomData<T>: a type marker that stores no values"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Rc\nnot Send","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Arc, Mutex\nSend + Sync","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"T: Sized","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"T: ?Sized\n(str, [T], dyn)","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["struct Id<T> { n: u32, _m: PhantomData<T> }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.7,29.5]}]},{"title":"Any","sub":"Dynamic types","short":"Any","main":"downcast_ref, TypeId, type_name.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["dyn Any","downcast_ref","type_name"],"captions":["Any: find a value's type while the program runs","downcast_ref::<T>() → Option<&T>: turns &dyn Any into a concrete type","TypeId and type_name: compare and name types; often an enum or trait is better: static check"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let v: Box<dyn Any> = Box::new(5i32);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["if let Some(n) = v.downcast_ref::<i32>() { }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["std::any::type_name::<T>()   // \"i32\""],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.6,29.6]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: asynchrony.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Catalog","Rule","Next"],"captions":["Clone, Copy, Eq, Ord, Hash, Default, From, AsRef, Deref, Iterator, Fn, Error, Send, Sync, Any","Derive whatever you can; implement by hand for special behavior","Next section is asynchrony: Python asyncio and async Rust with tokio"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Clone","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Ord","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"From","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Iterator","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"derive","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"manual impl","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":250.0,"h":34.0,"text":"async · await · tokio","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[25.6,31.8]}]}]}